model {
  extend basalt {
    stageCloudflare = module "Test stage account API" {
      #basalt
      description "The one deployment provider caller for isolated test stages, shared by the scale test and the emulated upstream and open to any further stage tool without a copy. A caller names its stage prefix, and optionally a predicate that narrows it, and gets back operations, never paths, URLs or credentials: the stage's container applications, runtime adapters and their namespaces (a namespace is owned through the runtime adapter that defines it and goes with it, so it is listed but never addressed), database connection configs and client certificates listed account-wide at once; a read, patch, rollout or delete of a row that listing returned, or a runtime adapter's settings by its name; the account's Worker subdomain; the image references the account's container applications run; and the stage's registry repositories with their tags, deleted index first. Every operation is one structured request to a single choke point, the only code that holds the network client. The choke point is built from a registered prefix and derives the ownership test itself; it accepts no ownership test from its caller. A request is a declared kind, a declared operation of that kind, a listed row or adapter name, and a body. It builds each URL from a fixed template per kind and operation and refuses before sending unless every name in it is inside the stage's registered prefix and no name the release stack's records use, and every id or registry reference is one this stage's own listing recorded for that name, unchanged since and free of separators, dots, escapes, query, fragment and whitespace. A resource addressed by an opaque id is read back by that id before it is read, changed or deleted, and the request is refused unless the answer names the recorded, owned name; a runtime adapter is addressed only by its own name. Short-lived registry credentials are minted, held and used inside the choke point and never returned. Every answer is read once, from a real HTTP response through its own accessors, into a snapshot of plain JSON with no prototypes; anything else is refused. Every internal table has no prototype, and every request field, option and answer field is read as the object's own, so a field set on the shared object prototype changes no request. Account-wide reads take nothing from the caller, and their rows are filtered by ownership before they are returned. Construction refuses a prefix that holds a release stage word, starts like a release stack name or is not registered, and a predicate that accepts a release stack name. Tests check that exactly one call of the network client exists in the module; enumerate every export of every file, every declared kind and operation and every key of the stage API, with the non-operation keys held to a fixed list and every operation given at least one hostile case, so an uncovered one fails; send each hostile input (dot segments, escaped separators, absolute paths and URLs, query and fragment characters, rows changed after listing or of another kind, look-alike prefixes and production names, listings whose rows carry another resource's id, answers that are not HTTP responses) against a recorded-shapes account whose every received URL is judged against the stage's own resources; and run every operation with each field the module reads set on the shared object prototype, requiring the same requests and answers as without. Every account read fails closed: a refused call, a false success envelope or a listing without its array throws, so a wrong template or a missing permission never reads as an empty account. Only a read of one resource answers absent, on 404. Refusals carry the operation, status, error codes and known field names, never remote messages. It holds no credential of its own."
      metadata {
        code "scripts/stage-cloudflare"
      }
    }
  }
  basalt.stageCloudflare -[sync]-> deploymentProvider "list, read back by id, patch, roll out and delete only a stage's own resources, and mint short-lived registry credentials it keeps, failing closed on any refusal"
  basalt.stageCloudflare -[sync]-> containerRegistry "list a stage's own repositories and tags and delete their manifests"
  basalt.scaleTest -[sync]-> basalt.stageCloudflare "find, change and delete only the scale stage's resources"
  basalt.emulatedUpstream -[sync]-> basalt.stageCloudflare "find and delete only the emulated stage's resources and registry images"
}
